window.docContents[40].resolve({"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Basic/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___Basic-1-0":{"contents":"Homogeneous polynomials\n\nThroughout, \\mathbb K is \\mathbb R or \\mathbb C (an RCLike field) and X, Y are normed spaces over \\mathbb K. A continuous n-homogeneous polynomial P\\colon X\\to Y is a map of the form P(x)=L(x,\\ldots,x) for some continuous n-linear map L (IsHomPoly). Its norm is the supremum over the closed unit ball,\n\\|P\\| = \\sup_{\\|x\\|\\le 1}\\|P(x)\\|\n(polyNorm). This module collects the elementary facts about diagonals of multilinear maps and their symmetrizations used everywhere else.\n\n\n","context":"","header":"LindenstraussPolynomials.Basic","id":"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Basic/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___Basic-1-0"}});